# Every input of the static FFmpeg build (task SPK-15), pinned by SHA-256. The Dockerfile downloads
# exactly these files, refuses any whose checksum differs, and bundles all of them with the recipe
# into the corresponding source archive. How the pins were established: README.md "Pins".
#
# Format: one entry per line, fields separated by blanks (no field contains a blank); lines starting
# with "#" and empty lines are ignored. Read by scripts/fetch-sources.sh and scripts/package.sh.
#
#   1  name     component name; NAME_VERSION and NAME_FILE variables use it upper-cased, "-" -> "_"
#   2  version  upstream release (or branch head for x264, commit for musl-cross-make)
#   3  stage    build stage that unpacks it: host, toolchain, libs or ffmpeg; also the
#               directory below sources/ in the source archive
#   4  linked   yes = code of it ends up in ffmpeg/ffprobe (libgcc is part of gcc); no = build tool
#   5  file     file name below sources/<stage>/
#   6  sha256   lowercase SHA-256 of that file
#   7  url      https download URL
#
# name           version     stage     linked file                                                          sha256                                                           url
nasm             2.16.03     host      no     nasm-2.16.03.tar.xz                                           1412a1c760bbd05db026b6c0d1657affd6631cd0a63cddb6f73cc6d4aa616148 https://www.nasm.us/pub/nasm/releasebuilds/2.16.03/nasm-2.16.03.tar.xz
